## Spatial, temporal, textural, transition, pressure/release, and recurrence maps

- **Spatial:** humidity is a reflective front plane; ginger cuts diagonally; violet textile hangs in the middle; mineral air opens behind it; cedar is the back wall; vetiver descends; Romandolide folds around, not over, the structure.
- **Temporal:** 0–5 min reflective ginger; 5–30 min green mineral seam; 30–120 min suspended violet/orris; 2–6 h mineral-air release into cedar; 6–24 h root-dry cloth recurrence. **NOT TESTED**.
- **Nineteen textures:** polished; waxed; wet-cut; reflective; crisp; fatty; fibrous; tailored-cloth; leafy; metallic; bitter; humid; mineral; pencil-dry; rooty; suede-soft; creamy-yielding; skin-like; slow.
- **Pressure/release:** humidity presses forward; ginger punctures; textile suspends; mineral air releases; cedar receives; sandal yields; vetiver lands; Romandolide folds.
- **Ten links:** (1) reflection→ginger, (2) ginger→green seam, (3) seam→violet glint, (4) glint→violet body, (5) body→orris lining, (6) lining→mineral air, (7) air→cedar, (8) cedar→sandal yield, (9) sandal→vetiver landing, (10) pear-skin musk→cloth recurrence.

