## Future mixing order

If later authorized: (1) salicylate, woods, vetivers, sandal, and Romandolide; (2) Suederal and ionone cloth; (3) floral/mineral air; (4) green and trace mineral seams; (5) ginger; (6) bergamot last; (7) alcohol phase. No ideal-only material and no omitted Benzyl Benzoate/Clearwood enters this executable order. Record stocks, masses, order, temperature, clarity, and losses. **No compounding is authorized.**

## Controlled blinded test plan

Compare current stock-corrected L'Homme V6 with LH-05 as independent constant-total 6,000 uL concentrates at matched final concentration and verified carrier composition. Use two independently prepared complete sets, anonymous codes, AB/BA counterbalance, equal substrates, and free description before scoring at 0, 5, 30, 120 minutes, 6 hours, and 24 hours. If the carriers of Damascol, Damascenone, Suederal, or Scentenal cannot be verified and matched, mark the physical test **HOLD** rather than infer equivalence.

Score separately: opening pleasure, humid reflection, ginger incision, violet-textile richness, orris lining, mineral-air release, cedar landing, root dryness, transition pleasure, drydown pleasure, overall liking, re-smell desire, muddiness, melon, detergent, metallic glare, and emptiness. One assay cannot prove safety, stability, or release.

